node_modules/
# Any .env* - the live file, its backups (.env.bak, .env.save) and local
# copies. The one exception is the template. Your CROWNS_WALLET_KEY lives in
# a file like this: a key that reaches a commit is a key you have to rotate.
.env*
!.env.example

# What the two doors write while you play - never source, never yours to
# commit. Not anchored to a directory on purpose: the client writes where
# CROWNS_OUT_DIR points, and the journal is named by CROWNS_CALL_LOG, so
# neither the depth nor the exact name is ours to predict.
*.apikey
*.lock
wallet*.json
*.log
crowns-response-*.json
